  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Friday 15 May 1936. Contests were threatened in both wards, but a last-minute compromise led four candidates to withdraw, leaving twelve for twelve seats: seven Nationalists, four Unionists and one Independent (Belfast News-Letter, 6 and 7 May 1936, pp. 9 and 15). Ten were nominated for seven seats; two Nationalists withdrew, leaving the seven named (3 Nat., 3 U., 1 Ind.). Returned unopposed."
